.TP
\fB~/.cline/data/settings/cline_mcp_settings.json\fR
Cline MCP server definitions. Vet reads flat servers and nested transport
objects, including nested env and headers. ClineStateShape reports a root or
an mcpServers value that is not an object; an empty mcpServers object is
valid. CLINE_MCP_SETTINGS_PATH replaces this file path. Relocate the data
directory with CLINE_DATA_DIR, otherwise CLINE_DIR/data (default
~/.cline/data). Vet inspects each path component before opening it, follows
local links, and refuses links to network shares; it reports SymlinkLoop after
eight links, NotARegularFile for a non\-regular file, and NetworkPathRefused
for a network target. ClineOverrideAlias reports a Cline row vet skips because
it is the same file as another vetted row: an overridden row that names any
other row's file, a content row that is a credential store at its default
location, or the later of two Cline files linked to each other. The other row
is read as usual unless it is also an override naming the same file, in which
case both rows are skipped. A credential store is never opened through any
Cline row.
.TP
\fB~/.cline/data/globalState.json\fR
Cline extension state. Vet reads only the eight autoApprovalSettings.actions
booleans: executeSafeCommands is HIGH because the extension's reader applies
it to every command tool; editFiles, useMcp, and useBrowser are MEDIUM;
readFiles is LOW. The legacy keys executeAllCommands, readFilesExternally, and
editFilesExternally have no shipped runtime reader and produce no finding.
False values produce no finding. Vet reports what the file declares: a default
install that persists its true defaults reports three MEDIUM findings and one
LOW finding. ClineStateShape reports a root, autoApprovalSettings, or actions
value that is not an object, or a known action that is not a boolean; vet
still reads the remaining known actions. Relocate the data directory with
CLINE_DATA_DIR, otherwise CLINE_DIR/data (default ~/.cline/data). Vet inspects
each path component before opening it, follows local links, and refuses links
to network shares; it reports SymlinkLoop after eight links, NotARegularFile
for a non\-regular file, and NetworkPathRefused for a network target.
ClineOverrideAlias reports a Cline row vet skips because it is the same file
as another vetted row: an overridden row that names any other row's file, a
content row that is a credential store at its default location, or the later
of two Cline files linked to each other. The other row is read as usual unless
it is also an override naming the same file, in which case both rows are
skipped. A credential store is never opened through any Cline row.
.TP
\fB~/.cline/data/settings/global\-settings.json\fR
Cline CLI settings. Vet reads only toolAutoApprove; true is HIGH and false
produces no finding. A CLI with no persisted value auto\-approves every tool
by default but declares nothing on disk, so vet reports nothing there.
ClineStateShape reports a root that is not an object or a toolAutoApprove
value that is not a boolean. CLINE_GLOBAL_SETTINGS_PATH replaces this file
path. Relocate the data directory with CLINE_DATA_DIR, otherwise
CLINE_DIR/data (default ~/.cline/data). Vet inspects each path component
before opening it, follows local links, and refuses links to network shares;
it reports SymlinkLoop after eight links, NotARegularFile for a non\-regular
file, and NetworkPathRefused for a network target. ClineOverrideAlias reports
