.TP
\fB./.clinerules/hooks/\fR
Cline project hook scripts. Vet reads this directory at the working directory,
the top of its git repository, and, in a linked worktree, the main checkout.
Vet reads each file whose name a loader for this directory accepts, whether or
not it is executable: the extension accepts the exact names TaskStart,
TaskResume, TaskCancel, TaskComplete, PreToolUse, PostToolUse,
UserPromptSubmit, Notification, and PreCompact, extensionless on macOS and
Linux and with .ps1 on Windows, and the SDK accepts TaskStart, TaskResume,
TaskCancel, TaskComplete, TaskError, PreToolUse, PostToolUse,
UserPromptSubmit, PreCompact, and SessionShutdown, case\-insensitively, with
no extension or one of .sh, .bash, .zsh, .js, .mjs, .cjs, .ts, .mts, .cts,
\&.py, and .ps1; vet rates each logical line, joining physical lines through a
backslash, backtick, or open\-quote continuation, an unclosed Python bracket,
or a trailing pipe, |&, or &&, and reports <file>:L<n> using the first
physical line number; it inspects each path component, follows local links,
and refuses network targets with NetworkPathRefused, reporting SymlinkLoop
after eight links along the whole path, the links that reach the hook
directory included, and NotARegularFile for a non\-regular file; it rates the
first 16 KiB and reports HookScriptTruncated for a longer file, counts
physical lines only in that prefix, including comments and blanks, and rates
the first 256 physical lines with HookScriptLineBudgetExceeded for further
lines; it rates an unfinished logical line at either limit, but does not rate
Python or JavaScript exfiltration through its own standard library with no
shell\-shaped string, or a command assembled from string literals split across
lines or joined with +. A JavaScript line whose code starts with // is a
comment; a trailing or block comment is still rated. A hook file that is the
same file as a credential store at its default location, which vet reads
stat\-only, is never read and is reported as ClineOverrideAlias, and so is
every hook while a credential store exists that vet cannot identify; a store
relocated by an override never stops a hook from being rated. Assess reads
this directory in the working directory's project and in every project Claude
Code records.
.TP
